    "body": "In this episode of Denatured, you’ll hear from Christina Smolke, co-founder & CEO at Antheia and Kyle Pudenz, senior vice president and head of data & AI product at Cencora. We explore why drug shortages are getting worse, and how combining predictive supply-chain analytics with agile, distributed manufacturing could finally make essential medicines more resilient and accessible.\n> Listen on Spotify > Listen on Apple Podcasts > Listen on Amazon Music > Listen on iheart > Watch on YouTube\nIn this episode of Denatured, you’ll listen to Christina Smolke, co-founder & CEO at Antheia and Kyle Pudenz, senior vice president and head of data & AI product at Cencora. We examine the factors driving the growing threat of drug shortages and explore how predictive supply chain insights, paired with flexible distributed manufacturing, can help strengthen medicine availability and improve patient access.\nHost\n⁠ Jennifer C. Smith-Parker , Director of Insights, BioSpace\nGuests\nChristina Smolke , Co-founder & CEO, Antheia\nKyle Pudenz , Senior Vice President, Head of Data & AI Product, Cencora\nDisclaimer: The views expressed in this discussion by guests are their own and do not represent those of their organizations.",
